[20.883326, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.883442, "o", "   3. The input file '\"'\"'/app/users.json'\"'\"' is fixed and will be used as input\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.883563, "o", "   4. The output will be redirected to '\"'\"'/app/active_users_report.json'\"'\"'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.883587, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.883672, "o", "   5. jq will be executed exactly once with all these components\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.883696, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>    \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.883714, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.883762, "o", "   Requirements for the YAML file:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[20.883785, "o", "> "]
[20.883933, "o", "   - The '\"'\"'args'\"'\"' list should contain complete jq arguments, with both flags and their values (if any)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[20.883974, "o", "> "]
[20.884021, "o", "   - Each argument should be a separate string in the list\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.884044, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[20.884068, "o", "> "]
[20.884175, "o", "   - For flag-only arguments, include just the flag (e.g., '\"'\"'--unbuffered'\"'\"', '\"'\"'--tab'\"'\"')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.8842, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.88437, "o", "   - For arguments with values, include both the flag and value as a single string (e.g., '\"'\"'--argjson min_count 5'\"'\"')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.884506, "o", "   - Do not include the jq command itself, the filter expression, or file paths in the args list\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.884547, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.884698, "o", "   - File paths other than the required input file '\"'\"'/app/users.json'\"'\"' and output redirections should not appear in the args\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.88472, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.884837, "o", "   - The filter should be a single string containing the complete jq filter expression\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.884864, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.884885, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.885265, "o", "**Note on examples below**: In the following Data Schema sections, all content following the '\"'\"'#'\"'\"' symbol is just explanatory commentary and will NOT appear in the actual JSON files. These comments are only provided to clarify the structure and requirements.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.885318, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> **Input Data Schema**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.88534, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.88547, "o", "The input JSON file '\"'\"'/app/users.json'\"'\"' is an array of user objects with the following structure:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.885504, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> [\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[20.885527, "o", ">   {\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.885624, "o", "    \"id\": 1,                  # Unique numeric identifier for the user\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.885648, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.885735, "o", "    \"username\": \"john_doe\",   # User'\"'\"'s unique username (string)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.885757, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.88585, "o", "    \"email\": \"john@example.com\",  # User'\"'\"'s email address (string)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.88586, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.886214, "o", "    \"status\": \"active\",       # User status: '\"'\"'active'\"'\"' or '\"'\"'inactive'\"'\"'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.886288, "o", "    \"last_login\": \"2024-10-02T20:59:10.109812Z\",  # ISO 8601 timestamp (UTC) of the last login\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.886387, "o", "    \"roles\": [\"admin\", \"editor\"]  # Array of roles assigned to the user (may be empty)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.886414, "o", "  },\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.886437, "o", "  ...\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[20.886461, "o", "> ]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.886485, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.88652, "o", "**Output Data Schema**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.88655, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.886697, "o", "The output JSON file '\"'\"'/app/active_users_report.json'\"'\"' must be an array of objects with the following structure:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.886719, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[20.886741, "o", "> [\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   {\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.886764, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.886858, "o", "    \"user_id\": 1,                 # Derived from '\"'\"'id'\"'\"' in input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.886877, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.886983, "o", "    \"username\": \"john_doe\",       # Retained from input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.887015, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.887099, "o", "    \"email\": \"john@example.com\",  # Retained from input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.887216, "o", "    \"last_login\": \"2024-10-02\",   # Formatted from '\"'\"'last_login'\"'\"' in input\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.887239, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.887332, "o", "    \"role_count\": 2,              # Count of '\"'\"'roles'\"'\"' from input\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.887355, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.887497, "o", "    \"primary_role\": \"admin\"       # If '\"'\"'roles'\"'\"' is empty, this must be null (JSON null, not \"null\")\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.887521, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>   },\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.887543, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>   ...\r\n"]
[20.887575, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[20.887598, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.88763, "o", "**Requirements**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.887652, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.887824, "o", "- You must use jq to perform this transformation. Using other programming languages (e.g., Python, Ruby) is strictly prohibited.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.887846, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.887953, "o", "- Ensure that the output JSON is properly formatted with 2-space indentation.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.887976, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.888097, "o", "- The output file must be created at the exact path '\"'\"'/app/active_users_report.json'\"'\"'.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.88812, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[20.888363, "o", "- The jq command used to generate the output(along with the output redirection) must be saved to '\"'\"'/app/cmd.sh'\"'\"'. This file will be used to verify the correctness of your solution.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[20.888388, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
